#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""Pearl pricing transaction journal and recovery (#1693, SPEC-023-R018 L4/L4b/L7).

A catalog-content release that changes rate-card rows replaces the
`rewards.rate_card` block of the live base coordinator.yaml together with the
autotune `current` release and `.previous-target` window, then SIGHUPs once.
This helper owns the on-host half of that transaction:

  begin / phase / install-candidate / check-state / restore-disk / finalize
      journal steps the lane runs, as children of its lease runner (the lane
      holds the updater + coordinator-deploy locks for the whole run).
  recover       operator recovery (catalog-content-release.sh
                --recover-pricing-txn), same locks, journal-only state.
  --pre-start   ExecStart of macprovider-coordinator-deploy-recovery.service,
                FIRST: restore the prior disk pair before the coordinator boots.
  --close-restored
                macprovider-coordinator-pricing-close.service: finalize a
                `restored-unverified` journal once the coordinator's boot
                record proves the prior pair is live.

State S = (base yaml sha, overlay presence+sha, `current` target, window
bytes|absent, digest set of the `current` release). Restore order is always
yaml, then `current`, then window. Every yaml write is same-directory temp +
file fsync + rename + parent fsync with explicit owner/group/mode.

Standard library only; run as `python3 -I`. Exit codes: 0 ok / nothing to do,
1 usage or refusal before any change, 3 state differs from the journal
(compare-and-swap refused; nothing further changed), 5 stopped with the
journal kept (follow docs/runbooks/catalog-release-decision-tree.md
§pricing-txn).
"""

